(*
PulseNode.ns — the Task 7 native_sim bring-up gate node. Deterministic
single-edge-then-loop: register a channel reaction, register + fire ONE
simulated GPIO edge (host/sim-only `gpio fire:`), then run the C-owned pump
loop. On native_sim the zephyr pulse backend's `pulse_pump`
(../src/backend/zephyr/pulse_zephyr.c) blocks (K_FOREVER) once the one-edge
mailbox is drained — the process prints the observation and then idles. That
is expected; the gate is checked under `timeout`, not by process exit.

Baked into a boot image with:
  python3 tools/ns_compile_oevm.py zephyr/PulseNode.ns src/solidified_image.c
(run from the nsl-tuvm repo — see zephyr/README.md for the exact commands).

Deviations from the plan's draft node (both required to actually compile/run
against this VM+compiler, not stylistic):
  - `[ ... ] repeat` is not a supported selector in this dialect (no `repeat`
    unary send exists anywhere in tools/ns_compile_oevm.py's compiler or in
    src/dispatch.c's PRIM_NAMES — only whileTrue:/whileFalse:/timesRepeat:/
    to:do:/to:by:do: are). Rewritten as the equivalent `[ true ] whileTrue:`.
  - the posted message is the String 'done', not the Symbol #done: a genuine
    Symbol's `printString` prints with a leading '#' (src/dispatch.c's
    PRIM_printString), which would print `observed #done` — NOT matching the
    required `observed done` substring. A String prints as itself.
*)
class PulseNode packageUsing: manifest = () (
  public main: platform args: args = (
    | space alert gpio |
    space:: platform space.
    alert:: space channel: 'sensor/alert'.
    alert whenever: '' do: [ :e | ('observed ' , e printString) out ].
    gpio:: platform gpio.
    gpio pin: 13 edge: #rising post: 'done' on: alert.
    gpio fire: 13.                                    (* sim: one edge *)
    [ true ] whileTrue: [ platform pumpEvents. space drain ]
  )
) : (
)
